These four In-Between spirits had no kingdoms of their own. They existed only in the transitions, the moments when one Season passed the world to another.

At first, the Seasons pitied them. "You have no realm to rule," Winter said sadly.

But Bloom laughed. "We rule the most magical times! When your colors mix, when neither yesterday nor tomorrow fully claims the day—that is our domain."

The In-Between spirits taught the world that change itself could be a destination, not just a journey. They showed that the moments of uncertainty—when one chapter ends and another begins—hold their own unique beauty and purpose.

Now, people celebrate these transition times: the first warm day, the first fallen leaf, the first snow, the first crocus. The In-Between spirits remind us that transformation, not permanence, is life's greatest gift.

